{"findings":[{"rule_id":"MF-007","evidence":[{"kind":"title_block","ref":"material","page":1,"quote":"Polyurethene"},{"kind":"title_block","ref":"surface_treatment","page":1,"quote":"I.Z.B.P. (TRIVALENT)"}],"comment":"The title block specifies the material as polyurethane but calls for I.Z.B.P. (trivalent zinc plating), a metallic surface treatment that cannot be applied to a polymer. The designer must correct either the material or the surface treatment so they are compatible."

,
"recommended_correction":"Remove the zinc plating callout if the part is polyurethane, or change the material if zinc plating is required."}]}
